preConditionHook:
// The structural gate under every opening-bar setup: this bar is the first
// bar of the session, i.e. its wall-clock close date differs from the
// previous bar's.
//
// SESSION MODEL, per the standing decision: the EasyLanguage twin's
// date > date[1], mirrored as day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1)).
// EL_Date_Probe.txt measured Date as the bar's wall-clock close date (169/169 bars, 50
// of them evening bars) and the xxxD family slices the calendar the same
// way, so one boundary serves both. ctx.Time(1) is the DATA series' real
// history -- MaxBarsBack bars exist before the first evaluated bar -- so no
// first-bar guard is needed, exactly as CalendarBoundaryExit relies on.
//
// The comparison is on integer day serials, not prices, so it is exact and
// does not go through el_gt; the boolean lands in a local because a rule
// CONDITION may not carry a raw relational operator.
//
// Direction-agnostic, so both sides are identical text. Intraday bars only.
newSess = day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1));
